Conclusion: on BASE (pre-round-98, plasma checkout), the one-range
NASA.to_cantera() case raises a bare AssertionError (not the named
CanteraThermoWriteError), and CanteraThermoWriteError does not exist at all
in rmgpy.exceptions -- so test_rmgpy/thermo/nasaTest.py's new
test_to_cantera_refuses_* tests fail at collection time (ImportError) on
base, and test_to_cantera_one_range would fail with AssertionError if the
import were patched around. This is the documented RED state.
